IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ca-founder`

-- Corporations Act 2001 (Cth) -- worked cases, from the seat of the founder-director and shareholder (Daniel).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case, an ASIC form or regulatory guide, or the Corporations Regulations 2001 (not deposited).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table (scratchpad gen_corporations-act-2001_baseline.py). Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from Daniel's life (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel): d043 (2031-03-15) Jarrah Legal
-- Technologies Pty Ltd registered, 70% Daniel, 10% Priya, 20% a sophisticated investor for $500,000; d050 (2035-09-01)
-- Series A, $5,000,000 for 25% from a fund; d064 (2042-03-31) a selective buy-back of the investor's shares; d065
-- (2043-06-15) Jarrah acquires Formly; d071 (2050-06-30) Jarrah sold to a listed buyer for $40,000,000; d073
-- (2051-09-01) non-executive director of a listed company; d081 (2056-03-20) angel investments as a sophisticated
-- investor.
-- ENCODER'S ASSUMPTIONS, not in the life: Daniel is Jarrah's sole director until the Series A; founders' shares were
-- issued for $70 (Daniel) and $10 (Priya); Priya is not a director or senior manager; the vote split after the Series A
-- (Daniel 525, Priya 75, investor 150, fund 250 of 1,000 votes); the fund's gross assets ($100,000,000); Jarrah's
-- members in 2050 (4); Daniel's net and gross assets in 2056 ($30,000,000); every certificate date, vote and figure
-- marked "variant". The s 708(8)(c) amounts ($2,500,000 net assets, $250,000 gross income) are HYPOTHETICAL inputs: the
-- Act leaves them to regulations that are not deposited.

